---
type: agent/instruction
description: Create a linked worktree and hand it to a fresh agent session
usage: "guide://_worktree/new[/<branch-name>]"
requires-handoff-context: true
requires-worktree-support: true
includes:
  - ../_partials/handoff-context-target
  - ../../_system/_handoff-context
elicitation:
  branch-name:
    message: "Choose the branch for the new worktree. An existing branch will be checked out; a new branch will be created from main."
    fallback: render
    schema:
      type: object
      properties:
        branch:
          type: string
      required: [branch]
---
{{#elicit.branch-name}}
{{h1}}Create linked worktree

{{>handoff-context}}

Guide allocated the worktree name `{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`.

1. Acquire the shared handoff-context lock as instructed above. If
   `projects.{{project.name}}.worktrees.{{kwargs.worktree_name}}` already
   exists, release the lock without creating a worktree or changing the
   handoff, then request `guide://_worktree/new` again. Otherwise retain the
   lock while completing the next step.
2. Create the linked worktree at `{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`.
   {{#args.0.value}}Use branch `{{args.0.value}}`.{{/args.0.value}}{{^args.0.value}}Use branch `{{kwargs.branch}}`.{{/args.0.value}}
   If that branch already exists, check it out. Otherwise create it from `main`,
   never from the current branch:
   ```sh
   git worktree add {{#shell_quote}}{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}{{/shell_quote}} -b {{#shell_quote}}{{#args.0.value}}{{args.0.value}}{{/args.0.value}}{{^args.0.value}}{{kwargs.branch}}{{/args.0.value}}{{/shell_quote}} main
   ```
   For an existing branch, use `git worktree add {{#shell_quote}}{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}{{/shell_quote}} {{#shell_quote}}{{#args.0.value}}{{args.0.value}}{{/args.0.value}}{{^args.0.value}}{{kwargs.branch}}{{/args.0.value}}{{/shell_quote}}` instead.
3. Create or initialise the new worktree's effective configured workflow file
   with `worktree: {{kwargs.worktree_name}}` before assigning the child. Preserve
   its workflow state and use the configured basename-only workflow filename.
4. Add the new entry at
   `projects.{{project.name}}.worktrees.{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, including
   the required `timestamp` and `path`, the selected branch, and instructions
   for the child. If worktree creation fails, release the lock without changing
   the handoff.
5. Hand the child the allocated worktree name `{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, the
   absolute path `{{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, and the complete
   handoff entry. Do not forward this session ID. Before binding Guide, the child
   must work from that path and read its local configured workflow file before
   any workflow or handoff-context operation. It must then create a fresh Guide interaction, bind
   `path: {{project.root}}` and
   `worktree: {{project.root}}_{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, submit that local
   workflow file, and read its own handoff entry before continuing.
{{/elicit.branch-name}}
